==Trivia==
*Glucosamine Desert and its stages are named after bioactive compounds that can be found in supplements.
**[[wikipedia:Glucosamine|Glucosamine]] is an [[wikipedia:Amino sugar|amino sugar]] that is a component of cartilage.
**[[wikipedia:Chondroitin|Chondroitin]] is another substance in cartilage, and it is commonly used in combination with glucosamine.
**[[wikipedia:Sesamin|Sesamin]] is included in supplements as an antioxidant and for its anti-inflammatory effects.
**[[wikipedia:Isoflavone|Isoflavone]] is sold as a dietary supplement.
**[[wikipedia:Catechin|Catechin]] is an [[wikipedia:Antioxidant|antioxidant]].
**[[wikipedia:Lycopene|Lycopene]] is a [[wikipedia:Carotenoid|carotenoid]] that is found in red and pink fruits and vegetables.
**[[wikipedia:Propolis|Propolis]] is thought to support the immune system.
**[[wikipedia:Peptide|Peptides]] are chains of [[wikipedia:Amino acid|amino acids]].
**[[wikipedia:Hyaluronic acid|Hyaluronan]] can be used for skin care and treatment of joints.

